@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why a package exists for one type, and why the interface it was created for is never written
' covers: internal/backend/backend.go
'
' ── ONE TYPE, AND THAT IS THE FINISHED STATE ───────────────────────────────
' The package was created during the cmd/proveo decomposition to hold what the
' two backends share, with a Plan(RunSpec)/Execute(Plan) interface promised once
' RunSpec existed. RunSpec now exists. THE INTERFACE IS STILL NOT WRITTEN, and
' the promise is withdrawn rather than left standing.
'
' Nothing consumes the backends polymorphically. run.selectBackend branches on
' which one won and calls each by name, because their shapes genuinely differ:
' sandbox.Run takes an Input and runs, while dockeregress splits into Assemble
' then Exec so the caller can start a review gate BETWEEN the two. An interface
' over two divergent implementers with no caller holding one describes nothing —
' it guesses a shape, which is the abstraction Go's own advice says to declare at
' the CONSUMER once a consumer exists.
'
' ── WHY THE PACKAGE STAYS ANYWAY ───────────────────────────────────────────
' Not for abstraction — for dependency direction. ExitError is needed by
' cmd/proveo and by BOTH backends. Put it in either backend and the other has to
' import its sibling; put it in cmd/proveo and internal/ imports cmd/. A leaf
' package is the only placement that leaves the graph acyclic.
'
' ── WHAT THE TYPE ACTUALLY GUARDS ──────────────────────────────────────────
' proveo's exit status must be the AGENT's, not proveo's own. A backend returns
' ExitError from deep inside a run and main recovers it with errors.As, so a CI
' step sees what the agent decided. The value must therefore survive wrapping:
' TestExitErrorSurvivesWrapping pins that, because a type that stopped matching
' through a %w chain would silently turn every agent failure into exit 1 and no
' test of the happy path would notice.
title internal/backend — a package for dependency direction, not abstraction

participant "sandbox" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "dockeregress" as DOC <<cloud>>
participant "backend.ExitError" as EE <<data>>
participant "cmd/proveo main" as MAIN <<app>>

SBX ARROW_ERROR EE : agent exited 137
DOC ARROW_ERROR EE : agent exited 1
EE ARROW_MAIN MAIN : errors.As through the wrap chain
MAIN ARROW_MAIN MAIN : os.Exit(code) — the AGENT's code

note over EE
  **No Plan/Execute interface.** Two implementers
  with different shapes and no caller that holds
  one. Declared at the consumer, if a consumer
  ever appears.
end note
@enduml
